    "Description": "The kernel packages contain the Linux kernel, the core of any Linux operating system.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* kernel: scsi: scsi_debug: Fix out-of-bound read in resp_readcap16() (CVE-2021-47191)\n\n* kernel: scsi: scsi_debug: Sanity check block descriptor length in resp_mode_select() (CVE-2021-47576)\n\n* kernel: s390/cpum_sf: Handle CPU hotplug remove during sampling (CVE-2024-57849)\n\n* kernel: drm/amdkfd: Fix out-of-bounds write in kfd_event_page_set() (CVE-2026-43206)\n\n* kernel: netfilter: nf_queue: hold bridge skb-\u003edev while queued (CVE-2026-52912)\n\n* kernel: drm/amd/display: Clamp VBIOS HDMI retimer register count to array size (CVE-2026-53136)\n\n* kernel: drm/amd/display: Use krealloc_array() in dal_vector_reserve() (CVE-2026-53329)\n\n* kernel: drm/amdgpu: zero-initialize GART table on allocation (CVE-2026-53374)\n\n* kernel: net: ip_gre: require CAP_NET_ADMIN in the device netns for changelink (CVE-2026-63829)\n\n* kernel: tunnels: do not assume transport header in iptunnel_pmtud_check_icmp() (CVE-2026-63992)\n\n* kernel: tunnels: load network headers after skb_cow() in iptunnel_pmtud_build_icmp[v6]() (CVE-2026-63994)\n\n* kernel: scsi: target: iscsi: Bound iscsi_encode_text_output() appends to rsp_buf (CVE-2026-63887)\n\n* kernel: net/smc: reject CHID-0 ACCEPT that matches an empty ism_dev slot (CVE-2026-64048)\n\n* kernel: drm/amd/display: Validate payload length and link_index in dc_process_dmub_aux_transfer_async (CVE-2026-64219)\n\n* kernel: net/iucv: fix use-after-free of a severed iucv_path (CVE-2026-68140)\n\n* kernel: vxlan: require CAP_NET_ADMIN in the device netns for changelink (CVE-2026-68432)\n\n* kernel: net: ip6_gre: require CAP_NET_ADMIN in the device netns for changelink (CVE-2026-72052)\n\n* kernel: netfilter: nf_queue: pin bridge device while NFQUEUE holds fake dst (CVE-2026-72255)\n\n* kernel: netfilter: nf_conntrack_sip: widen NAT rewrite delta to s32 in sip_help_tcp() (CVE-2026-74569)\n\n* kernel: netfilter: nf_conntrack: use get_unaligned_be32() in tcp_sack() (CVE-2026-97417)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
